        'advice.win11Ready'        = 'Make a backup first, then upgrade through Windows Update or Microsoft''s Installation Assistant. Files and programs stay; it takes 1 to 2 hours.'
        'steps.win11Ready'         = 'Make a backup first: copy Documents, Pictures and Desktop to a USB drive, or check that OneDrive has them. | Plug in the charger (laptop) and make sure the internet works. | Choose the fix to open Windows Update. Is "Upgrade to Windows 11" offered there? Click Download and install. | Not offered? Choose the other fix: on Microsoft''s page, Windows 11 Installation Assistant, Download now, and run it. | The upgrade takes 1 to 2 hours and restarts a few times; files and programs stay. | Afterwards: check that the printer, email and online banking still work.'
        'finding.win11TpmOff'      = 'The security chip (TPM 2.0) is not found. On most PCs from 2017 or later it is there, but switched off in the BIOS.'
        'advice.win11TpmOff'       = 'Switch it on in the BIOS: on AMD it is called fTPM, on Intel PTT or Platform Trust Technology. Then run this check again.'
        'steps.win11TpmOff'        = 'Save open work and restart the PC. | While it starts, press the BIOS key (often Del, F2, F10 or F1; the maker''s logo screen says which). | Look under Security, Advanced or Trusted Computing for TPM, fTPM (AMD) or PTT / Platform Trust Technology (Intel). | Set it to Enabled, then Save and exit (often F10). | Back in Windows, run E4 again.'
        'finding.win11Legacy'      = 'The PC starts the old way (Legacy BIOS). Windows 11 needs UEFI.'
        'advice.win11Legacy'       = 'Converting is possible without losing files (Microsoft''s MBR2GPT tool, then the BIOS to UEFI), but it is technical: plan it as a separate job, with a full backup first.'
        'steps.win11Legacy'        = 'Make a full backup of the client''s files first. | Plan it as a separate job: converting the disk (MBR2GPT) and switching the BIOS to UEFI takes care and time. | After that, switch on Secure Boot and TPM in the BIOS and run E4 again.'
        'finding.win11Space'       = 'Only {0} GB is free; the upgrade needs about 30 GB.'
        'advice.win11Space'        = 'Make room first: D4 shows what takes the space.'
        'steps.win11Space'         = 'Choose D4 to see what takes the space. | Empty the Recycle Bin and clear the temporary files there. | Move big videos and photos to a USB drive. | Run E4 again.'
        'finding.win11NotPossible' = 'This PC cannot run Windows 11: {0}.'
