        'steps.gpuNoDriver'        = 'Choose the fix to open the maker''s driver page. | Or: Windows Update > Advanced options > Optional updates > Driver updates. | Restart the PC afterwards.'
        'finding.gpuDriverOld'     = 'The graphics driver froze {0} time(s) in 30 days, and it is more than half a year old.'
        'advice.gpuDriverOld'      = 'Install the newest driver from the maker''s site first; many freezes are fixed there.'
        'steps.gpuDriverOld'       = 'Choose the fix to open the maker''s driver page and install the newest driver. | AMD: choose Factory Reset during the installation; NVIDIA: Custom > Clean installation. | Restart, then check again with B7 after a few days.'
        'finding.gpuResets'        = 'The graphics driver froze and restarted {0} time(s) in 30 days: that is the black screen, and why games crash.'
        'advice.gpuResets'         = 'Often when the mouse goes to another screen during a game: the game leaves full screen and the driver has to switch. Borderless windowed mode, hardware acceleration off in apps on the other screen, and equal screen speeds usually solve it.'
        'steps.gpuResets'          = 'In each game choose Borderless window (or Windowed fullscreen) instead of Full screen: then nothing has to switch when the mouse leaves. | Switch off hardware acceleration in programs on the other screen: Spotify (Settings > Compatibility), Discord, the browser. | Pause a moving wallpaper (Wallpaper Engine) while gaming. | Screens at different speeds? Turn FreeSync/G-Sync off on the second screen, or set it to a speed the first one divides by (Advanced display). | Install the newest driver cleanly from the maker''s page (AMD: Factory Reset). | Still happening? Check the power cables of the graphics card and the power supply: a repair job.'
        'finding.gpuHardware'      = 'Windows reported {0} serious hardware error(s) in 30 days.'
        'advice.gpuHardware'       = 'Usually the processor or memory running beyond what is stable (an overclock, XMP/EXPO memory profile), sometimes heat or a failing part.'
        'steps.gpuHardware'        = 'Overclocked, or XMP/EXPO on in the BIOS? Set it back to default and see if the errors stop. | Update the BIOS from the maker of the motherboard. | Still errors? Test the memory and the processor: a repair job.'
        'finding.gpuOk'            = 'The graphics driver did not freeze in 30 days.'
        'advice.gpuOk'             = 'A black screen anyway? Check the cable and the screen''s input, and try another port.'
        'steps.gpuOk'              = 'Press the cable in firmly at both ends, or try another cable. | Choose the right input on the screen (HDMI 1, DisplayPort). | Does one game crash? Check its files in its launcher (Steam: Verify integrity).'
