        'finding.unexpectedOff'    = 'The PC switched off without shutting down {0} time(s) in 30 days.'
        'advice.unexpectedOff'     = 'Usually power (a loose plug, a power strip, a worn laptop battery) or heat (dust in the fan). Rarely the power supply itself.'
        'steps.unexpectedOff'      = 'Ask the client: does it happen when moving the cable, or when the PC is busy (a video, a game)? | Plug the PC straight into the wall, not via a power strip, and check the cable. | Laptop: choose C4 for the battery. | Feel whether it gets hot and listen to the fan: choose D6. | Keeps happening? The power supply may be failing: a repair job.'
        'finding.blueScreenRestarts' = 'The PC restarted after {0} blue screen(s) in 30 days.'
        'advice.blueScreenRestarts'  = 'A blue screen is a crash of Windows itself: often a driver or a memory fault. D3 shows more, and Windows Update often has the fix.'
        'steps.blueScreenRestarts'   = 'Choose D3 to see the crashes. | Install all updates and optional driver updates (E1). | Keeps happening? Test the memory: Windows Memory Diagnostic, from the Start menu.'
        'finding.updateRestarts'   = 'Windows Update restarted the PC {0} time(s) in 30 days.'
        'advice.updateRestarts'    = 'Set the active hours to when the client uses the PC; Windows then restarts outside them.'
        'steps.updateRestarts'     = 'Choose the fix to open the active hours. | Set them to when the client uses the PC, for example 8:00 to 23:00. | Tip for the client: restart once a week yourself; then Windows hardly needs to.'
        'finding.restartsOk'       = 'No unexpected power-offs or restarts in 30 days.'
        'advice.restartsOk'        = 'Does it go dark rather than off? Choose B4 (screen and sleep times).'
        'steps.restartsOk'         = 'Ask the client what exactly happens: black screen (B4), or really off? | Really off but not in the log: check the power cable and the power strip.'
        'finding.hotBusy'          = 'The processor is {0}% busy, mostly from {1}: that makes the PC warm and the fan loud.'
        'advice.hotBusy'           = 'Close that program if it is not needed now (unsaved work in it is lost). Is it busy all the time? Choose D1.'
        'steps.hotBusy'            = 'Choose the fix to close the busiest program, or close it yourself. | Listen whether the fan calms down after a minute. | Busy all the time? Choose D1, and F3 for a security check.'
        'finding.hotPlan'          = 'The laptop runs in the power plan "{0}": always at full speed.'
        'advice.hotPlan'           = 'Set it to Balanced (Windows 11: power mode Balanced): quieter, cooler, and the battery lasts longer.'
        'steps.hotPlan'            = 'Choose the fix to open Settings > Power. | Set the power mode to Balanced.'
        'finding.hotDust'          = 'Nothing is keeping the processor busy right now.'
        'advice.hotDust'           = 'Hot or loud anyway? Usually dust in the fan, or a laptop on a soft surface (bed, sofa) that blocks the air.'
        'steps.hotDust'            = 'Laptop: put it on a table, not on a bed or cushion: the air goes in underneath. | Look at the vents: dust? Blow it out with a can of air in short bursts, with the PC off. | Desktop: open the side panel and clean the fans (a separate job). | Still loud? The fan may be worn: a repair job.'
        'finding.installSMode'     = 'Windows is in S mode: only Store apps can be installed.'
        'advice.installSMode'      = 'Switching out of S mode is free but one way: it cannot be switched back. Do it only if the client needs a program from outside the Store.'
        'steps.installSMode'       = 'Ask the client whether the program is in the Microsoft Store: then install it there. | Not? Settings > System > Activation > Switch out of S mode > Go to the Store > Get. | Note: this cannot be undone.'
        'finding.installStoreOnly' = 'Only apps from the Microsoft Store may be installed.'
        'advice.installStoreOnly'  = 'Set "Choose where to get apps" to Anywhere, or to warn first, if the client needs this program.'
        'steps.installStoreOnly'   = 'Choose the fix to open Settings > Apps > Advanced app settings. | Set "Choose where to get apps" to "Anywhere, but let me know". | Try the installation again.'
        'finding.installNoSpace'   = 'Only {0} GB is free: too little to install.'
        'advice.installNoSpace'    = 'Make room first: D4 shows what takes the space.'
        'steps.installNoSpace'     = 'Choose D4 and clear temporary files and the Recycle Bin. | Try the installation again.'
        'finding.installMsiOff'    = 'The Windows Installer service is switched off, so many installers fail.'
        'advice.installMsiOff'     = 'Choose the fix below to switch it back on (needs an administrator window).'
        'steps.installMsiOff'      = 'Choose the fix above, or: Services, Windows Installer, startup type Manual. | Try the installation again.'
        'finding.installReboot'    = 'A restart is waiting for an update.'
        'advice.installReboot'     = 'Restart the PC first; installers often refuse until then.'
        'steps.installReboot'      = 'Save open work and restart the PC. | Try the installation again.'
        'finding.installNotAdmin'  = 'This account is not an administrator.'
        'advice.installNotAdmin'   = 'Many programs then ask for an administrator''s password. Ask who has it (a family member), or install from the Microsoft Store.'
        'steps.installNotAdmin'    = 'Ask who manages this PC and has the administrator password. | Or install the program from the Microsoft Store, which needs no administrator.'
        'finding.installSmartApp'  = 'Smart App Control is on and blocks programs it does not know.'
        'advice.installSmartApp'   = 'Good protection; switch it off only for a program the client trusts, and know that it cannot be switched on again without reinstalling Windows.'
        'steps.installSmartApp'    = 'Check that the program comes from the maker''s own website. | Windows Security > App and browser control > Smart App Control settings. | Switching it off cannot be undone: only for a trusted program.'
        'finding.installOk'        = 'Nothing on this PC blocks installing.'
        'advice.installOk'         = 'Still failing? Read the error message (a photo helps), and download the installer again from the maker''s own website.'
        'steps.installOk'          = 'Download the program again from the maker''s own website (not a download site). | Right-click the installer > Run as administrator. | Note the exact error message and search for it.'
        'finding.browserPolicy'    = '{0} is "managed by your organisation" on this home PC.'
        'advice.browserPolicy'     = 'On a home PC that is often a hijacker: it locks the search engine, start page or add-ons. On a work PC it is normal. Ask the client, then check the policies (a separate, careful job).'
        'steps.browserPolicy'      = 'Ask the client whether this PC is from work: then this is normal. | Not from work? Choose F3 for a full security check. | The policies are in the registry (Software\Policies): remove them only with a backup, as a separate job.'
        'finding.browserSearchHijack' = '{0} searches with {1}, not a search engine people pick themselves.'
        'advice.browserSearchHijack'  = 'That is how browser hijackers earn money. Reset the browser''s settings (bookmarks and passwords stay), and remove unknown add-ons.'
        'steps.browserSearchHijack'   = 'Choose the fix to open the reset page and confirm Reset settings. | Choose the fix for the add-ons and remove the ones the client does not know. | Then F3 for a full security check.'
        'finding.browserStartHijack'  = '{0} opens with {1}, a search page someone else chose.'
        'advice.browserStartHijack'   = 'Reset the browser''s settings: start page, search engine and add-ons go back to normal; bookmarks and passwords stay.'
        'steps.browserStartHijack'    = 'Choose the fix to open the reset page and confirm Reset settings. | Set the start page the client wants afterwards.'
        'finding.browserExtOutside'   = '{0} has add-ons that do not come from the store.'
        'advice.browserExtOutside'    = 'Most hijackers arrive as an add-on. Go through them with the client and remove what they do not know.'
        'steps.browserExtOutside'     = 'Choose the fix to open the add-ons. | Remove the ones the client does not know or use. | Afterwards: F3 for a full security check.'
        'finding.browserOk'        = 'The browsers search with a normal search engine, and no strange add-ons or policies were found.'
        'advice.browserOk'         = 'Still strange pages or pop-ups? Choose F1 for notification sites.'
        'steps.browserOk'          = 'Pop-ups that look like a virus warning: choose F1. | Firefox is not read: check its add-ons by hand (menu > Add-ons).'
        'problem.B6' = 'A second screen or TV shows nothing'
